\subsection{Statistical Validation}
\label{sec:stat-validation}

All significance tests use the nonparametric bootstrap with $B = 10{,}000$ resamples. Table~\ref{tab:bootstrap} presents confidence intervals for the severity gradient under both paired and unpaired analyses.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\caption{Bootstrap confidence intervals ($B{=}10{,}000$) for the severity gradient. Paired: same problem matched across strategies, controlling for problem-level variance. Unpaired: per-strategy gradient CI. All tests reject $H_0{:}\, G = 1$ at $p < 0.0001$.}
\label{tab:bootstrap}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lcccc@{}}
\toprule
$s$ & Paired $G$ & Paired 95\% CI & Unpaired $G$ & Unpaired 95\% CI \\
\midrule
0.15 & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_G_s015} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_lo_s015}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_hi_s015}] & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_G_s015} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_lo_s015}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_hi_s015}] \\
0.20 & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_G_s020} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_lo_s020}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_hi_s020}] & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_G_s020} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_lo_s020}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_hi_s020}] \\
0.25 & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_G_s025} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_lo_s025}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_hi_s025}] & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_G_s025} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_lo_s025}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_hi_s025}] \\
0.30 & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_G_s030} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_lo_s030}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: paired_CI_hi_s030}] & \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_G_s030} & [\placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_lo_s030}, \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: unpaired_CI_hi_s030}] \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The paired analysis---which controls for problem-level variance by matching the same problem across strategies---yields tighter intervals than the unpaired analysis, consistent with high between-problem variance in sequence length and II magnitude. Both paired and unpaired tests confirm that the importance-based gradient exceeds unity at every sparsity level ($p < 0.0001$).

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/fig4_bootstrap.pdf}
\caption{Forest plot of bootstrap severity gradient estimates. Horizontal bars show 95\% percentile CIs; diamonds mark point estimates. All importance-based CIs lie entirely above $G{=}1$ (vertical dashed line), confirming phase modulation at every sparsity level.}
\label{fig:bootstrap-forest}
\end{figure}

Permutation tests further validate the strategy dependence: under the null hypothesis that importance-based and random eviction produce equivalent severity gradients, the observed gradient difference at each sparsity level falls outside the permutation distribution ($p < 0.0001$; \placeholder{exp_id: deepseek_bf16_bootstrap, metric: n_valid_pairs} valid problem pairs after NaN filtering). Full per-problem distributions and permutation test details appear in Appendix~\ref{app:bootstrap-details}.

